Oh, Lord, that muItiplication error.

3
00:00:05,609 --> 00:00:07,779
(Sheldon:)He thought he carried the one,
but he didn't.

4
00:00:10,655 --> 00:00:12,745
(Leonard:)It's not funny.
That mistake got published.

5
00:00:12,949 --> 00:00:15,619
Stop, I'm gonna wet myseIf.

6
00:00:16,286 --> 00:00:18,746
Guys. Guys, President Seibert
is headed this way.

7
00:00:18,955 --> 00:00:21,245
l wonder what he wants.
- He doesn't look happy.

8
00:00:21,458 --> 00:00:22,748
I'm guessing he wants Sheldon.

9
00:00:22,959 --> 00:00:24,629
(Seibert:)- Dr. Cooper.
- Told you.

10
00:00:24,836 --> 00:00:26,296
Ah, President Seibert.

11
00:00:26,505 --> 00:00:28,215
(Sheldon:)I assume you'd like to respond...

12
00:00:28,423 --> 00:00:31,263
(Sheldon:)...to one of the suggestions
I put in the box by your office.

13
00:00:31,468 --> 00:00:34,678
(Seibert:)No, and stop installing
suggestion boxes everywhere.

14
00:00:35,305 --> 00:00:36,935
(Sheldon:)You don't like written suggestions.

15
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:40,100
(Sheldon:)You don't like when I give them
to you while in the men's room.

16
00:00:40,310 --> 00:00:43,440
(Sheldon:)If I didn't know any better,
I'd say you're one of those people...

17
00:00:43,647 --> 00:00:45,977
(Sheldon:)...who are not open to suggestions.

18
00:00:46,191 --> 00:00:49,861
(Seibert:)Dr. Cooper, the Physics Department
tells me you're refusing to take vacation.

19
00:00:50,070 --> 00:00:52,740
- I don't need a vacation.
- You're obligated to take one.

20
00:00:52,948 --> 00:00:55,868
And I'd like you to know
the most often received suggestion...

21
00:00:56,076 --> 00:00:58,866
(Seibert:)...in my suggestion box you installed
without asking me is:

22
00:00:59,079 --> 00:01:01,039
"Can Dr. Cooper take a vacation?"

23
00:01:02,165 --> 00:01:05,165
Okay, it's settled, then. I'll see you all
on Monday. Except for you.

24
00:01:05,377 --> 00:01:08,087
(Sheldon:)But if I don't come into work,
what am I supposed to do?

25
00:01:08,296 --> 00:01:10,546
(Seibert:)Read, rest, travel.

26
00:01:10,757 --> 00:01:13,257
(Seibert:)I hear Afghanistan is nice
this time of year.

27
00:01:15,470 --> 00:01:17,010
(Sheldon:)Sarcasm?

28
00:01:17,222 --> 00:01:21,022
(Howard:)No, you should go.

